{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Food you shall buy from them.</b> If they wish to sell. And there are those who say [it is] because the word is in the imperative [תשברו], and the meaning is that they have no need for food and drink these forty years that have passed, and the witness to this is כי ה' אלהיך ברכך (for YHWH your Elohim has blessed you)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The letter ו in וי״א is resolved as 'and'; the comment about תשברו being in the imperative (ת in temidiyyut, i.e. feminine/imperative form) is rendered literally; the implied 'forty' years is supplied from context in the word 'passed' though the Hebrew says simply 'these years that passed.'"}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:21:59.694022178Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}